{"title":"JEE Advanced","category":"Engineering","bank":"jee_advanced","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","count":9,"questions":[{"id":25949,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let<br><br>$\\alpha = \\left(1 - 2\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{11}\\right)\\right)\\left(1 - 2\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{11}\\right)\\right)\\left(1 - 2\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{9\\pi}{11}\\right)\\right)\\left(1 - 2\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{27\\pi}{11}\\right)\\right)\\left(1 - 2\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{81\\pi}{11}\\right)\\right)$.<br><br>Then the value of $5 - \\alpha^2$ is _____________.","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"Let the given expression be $\\alpha$. First, we simplify the angles in the product.<br><br>$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{27\\pi}{11}\\right) = \\cos\\left(2\\pi + \\dfrac{5\\pi}{11}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{11}\\right)$<br><br>$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{81\\pi}{11}\\right) = \\cos\\left(7\\pi + \\dfrac{4\\pi}{11}\\right) = -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}{11}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\pi - \\dfrac{4\\pi}{11}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{7\\pi}{11}\\right)$<br><br>Thus, the angles are $\\dfrac{\\pi}{11}, \\dfrac{3\\pi}{11}, \\dfrac{5\\pi}{11}, \\dfrac{7\\pi}{11}, \\dfrac{9\\pi}{11}$, which can be written as $\\theta_k = \\dfrac{(2k-1)\\pi}{11}$ for $k = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5$.<br><br>The expression becomes:<br>$\\alpha = \\prod_{k=1}^{5} \\left(1 - 2\\cos\\theta_k\\right)$<br><br>Using the trigonometric identity $1 - 2\\cos\\theta = 1 - 2(2\\cos^2(\\theta/2) - 1) = 3 - 4\\cos^2(\\theta/2)$.<br>Multiplying and dividing by $\\cos(\\theta/2)$, we get:<br>$1 - 2\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{3\\cos(\\theta/2) - 4\\cos^3(\\theta/2)}{\\cos(\\theta/2)} = -\\dfrac{\\cos(3\\theta/2)}{\\cos(\\theta/2)}$<br><br>Applying this identity to the product:<br>$\\alpha = \\prod_{k=1}^{5} \\left( -\\dfrac{\\cos(3\\theta_k/2)}{\\cos(\\theta_k/2)} \\right) = (-1)^5 \\dfrac{\\prod_{k=1}^{5} \\cos(3\\theta_k/2)}{\\prod_{k=1}^{5} \\cos(\\theta_k/2)}$<br><br>The terms in the denominator are $\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{7\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{9\\pi}{22}\\right)$.<br><br>The terms in the numerator are $\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{9\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{15\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{21\\pi}{22}\\right), \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{27\\pi}{22}\\right)$.<br><br>We can simplify the larger angles in the numerator:<br>$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{15\\pi}{22}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\pi - \\dfrac{7\\pi}{22}\\right) = -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{7\\pi}{22}\\right)$<br><br>$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{21\\pi}{22}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\pi - \\dfrac{\\pi}{22}\\right) = -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{22}\\right)$<br><br>$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{27\\pi}{22}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\pi + \\dfrac{5\\pi}{22}\\right) = -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{22}\\right)$<br><br>Substituting these back into the numerator product:<br>$\\prod_{k=1}^{5} \\cos(3\\theta_k/2) = \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{22}\\right) \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{9\\pi}{22}\\right) \\left(-\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{7\\pi}{22}\\right)\\right) \\left(-\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{22}\\right)\\right) \\left(-\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{22}\\right)\\right)$<br><br>$\\prod_{k=1}^{5} \\cos(3\\theta_k/2) = - \\left[ \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{22}\\right) \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{22}\\right) \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{22}\\right) \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{7\\pi}{22}\\right) \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{9\\pi}{22}\\right) \\right]$<br><br>Notice that the term in the brackets is exactly the denominator product. Therefore, the ratio of the numerator product to the denominator product is $-1$.<br><br>$\\alpha = (-1)^5 \\times (-1) = (-1) \\times (-1) = 1$<br><br>We need to find the value of $5 - \\alpha^2$:<br>$5 - (1)^2 = 5 - 1 = 4$<br><br>Answer: $4$","difficulty":"Hard","source":"JEE Advanced 2026 (Paper 1)","_marksId":"6a0be50d44d287c9361e5c83","questionType":"numerical","_advSection":"NUM","type":"numerical","correctValue":"4"},{"id":25950,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let $\\alpha=\\frac{1}{\\sin 60^{\\circ} \\sin 61^{\\circ}}+\\frac{1}{\\sin 62^{\\circ} \\sin 63^{\\circ}}+\\ldots+\\frac{1}{\\sin 118^{\\circ} \\sin 119^{\\circ}}$\nThen the value of $\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}{\\alpha}\\right)^2$ is __________","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"$\\begin{aligned} & \\alpha=\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}-30}^{59} \\frac{1}{\\sin (2 \\mathrm{r})^{\\circ} \\sin (2 \\mathrm{r}+1)^{\\circ}} \\\\ & \\frac{\\alpha}{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}=\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}-30}^{59} \\frac{\\sin 1^{\\circ}}{\\sin (2 \\mathrm{r})^{\\circ} \\sin (2 \\mathrm{r}+1)^{\\circ}} \\\\ & =\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}-30}^{59}\\left(\\cot (2 \\mathrm{r})^{\\circ}-\\cot (2 \\mathrm{r}+1)^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\ & =\\cot 60^{\\circ}-\\cot 61^{\\circ} \\\\ & \\quad+\\cot 62^{\\circ}-\\cot 63^{\\circ} \\\\ & \\quad \\vdots \\\\ & +\\cot \\left(118^{\\circ}\\right)-\\cot \\left(119^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\ & \\frac{\\alpha}{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}=\\cot 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ & \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}{\\alpha}\\right)^2=3\\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Hard","source":"JEE Advanced 2025 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"685102c26bba689a3eb09cad","questionType":"numerical","_advSection":"NUM","type":"numerical","correctValue":"3"},{"id":25951,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi></math> be real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo><</mo><mi>β</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn><mo><</mo><mi>α</mi><mo><</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, then the greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is","options":[],"answer":"1","solution":"<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>·</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>·</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>·</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>·</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p></blockquote>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JEE Advanced 2022 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a9ef23ac7d519f9b60e","_advSection":"NUM","questionType":"numerical","type":"numerical","correctValue":"1"},{"id":25952,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∞</mo></munderover><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></math> be the function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msup></math>. Then, which of the following statements is/are TRUE?","options":["The minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math>","The maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>","The function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> attains its maximum at more than one point","The function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> attains its minimum at more than one point"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∞</mo></munderover><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msup></math>. </p><p>Now solving,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∞</mo></munderover><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∞</mo></munderover><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now putting the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Now finding the critical point by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>And, derivative changes sign from negative to positive at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is point of local minimum as well as absolute minimum of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo></math> Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math> is correct</p><p>Now maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is either equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence (B) and (C) are also correct.</p>","difficulty":"Hard","source":"JEE Advanced 2022 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a9ff23ac7d519f9b617","_advSection":"MC","questionType":"multipleCorrect","type":"multipleCorrect","answers":[0,1,2]},{"id":25953,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"For non-negative integers <math><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></math> let<br  /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>n</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math><br  />Assuming <math><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math> takes values in <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> which of the following options is/are correct?","options":["<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math>","If <math><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>n</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi> </mi></mrow><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd/></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>∵</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>∵</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br  /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math><br  /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math><br  />Now <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>β</mi></mrow><mro