s 2 \\theta}=1+\\frac{1}{\\cos 2 \\theta}$\r\n\r\nLet $\\cos 4 \\theta=\\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow 2 \\cos ^{2} 2 \\theta-1=\\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow \\cos 2 \\theta=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\therefore f(\\cos 4 \\theta)=1+\\frac{1}{\\cos 2 \\theta}=1 \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}$ or $f\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=1 \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JEE Advanced 2012 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a24f23ac7d519f9b1bb","_advSection":"MC","questionType":"multipleCorrect","type":"multipleCorrect","answers":[0,1]},{"id":25957,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let $\\theta \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$ and $t_1=(\\tan \\theta)^{\\tan \\theta}, t_2=(\\tan \\theta)^{\\cot \\theta}$ and $t_4=(\\cot \\theta)^{\\tan \\theta}$, then","options":["$t_1\\gt t_2\\gt t_3\\gt t_4$","$t_4\\gt t_3\\gt t_1\\gt t_2$","$t_3\\gt t_1\\gt t_2\\gt t_4$","$t_2\\gt t_3\\gt t_1\\gt t_4$"],"answer":1,"solution":"As when $\\theta \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\tan \\theta \\lt  \\cot \\theta$\nSince, $\\tan \\theta \\lt  1$ and $\\cot \\theta\\gt 1\\therefore(\\tan \\theta)^{\\cot \\theta} \\lt  1$ and $(\\cot \\theta)^{\\tan \\theta}\\gt 1\\therefore t_4\\gt t_1$ which only holds in option (b).","difficulty":"Easy","source":"JEE Advanced 2006","_marksId":"64b169cdf23ac7d519f9ae9a","_advSection":"SC","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect"}]}